  "body": "## What was broken\n\nA caller that demanded a specific tool got a request that no longer demanded it.\n\n`_downgrade_forced_tool_choice` (`compat.py:420-433`) rewrote **every** Anthropic `tool_choice: {type:\"tool\", name:X}` to `{\"type\":\"auto\"}` while building the request body, logging only at `logger.debug`. The model was then free to answer in prose and call nothing — exactly the failure a forced tool choice exists to prevent — and nothing surfaced that the demand had been dropped.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe downgrade was **unconditional and up front**, applied to every DeepSeek request.\n\nBut [DeepSeek's API reference](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/create-chat-completion/) documents `tool_choice` accepting `\"none\"` | `\"auto\"` | `\"required\"` | a named function object — forced choice is a supported part of the general model surface. Only the *reasoning* models reject it, at request time with an HTTP 400 ([R1 #836](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1/issues/836), [R1 #813](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1/issues/813), [V3 #1376](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3/issues/1376)).\n\nDowngrading everything to protect one model class removed a documented capability from all of them.\n\n## The fix\n\nRemoves the up-front rewrite; handles rejection **reactively**, mirroring the existing sibling pattern in `mistral/client.py:58-68` — a narrow error predicate, a body clone, wired through the provider's `_get_retry_request_body` hook, logged at **WARNING**.\n\n```\nforced named choice  -> sent to DeepSeek unmodified\n   |\n   +-- rejected (400 mentioning tool_choice) -> retry once with tool_choice: \"required\"\n```\n\n`\"required\"` rather than `\"auto\"`: the caller demanded a tool call, so the must-call-*something* half survives even when the *which tool* half cannot be honoured.\n\n**Detection is on the returned error, never the model id.** DeepSeek's names have already shifted once (`deepseek-reasoner` → `deepseek-v4-pro/flash`), and branching on upstream model names is banned by CLAUDE.md. This also **self-heals** the day DeepSeek lifts the restriction — no list to maintain.\n\nThe predicate requires **both** an HTTP 400 **and** text mentioning `tool_choice` together with a rejection word, so unrelated 400s (context length, bad schema, invalid model) never trigger a downgrade. There is a test for exactly that.\n\n## Known limitation — documented, not hidden\n\nThe retry hook fires **at most once per request**. `_next_create_retry_body` adds `\"provider_specific\"` to `used_retry_kinds` and every later iteration skips the branch:\n\n```python\n# openai_chat/provider.py:340-345\nif \"provider_specific\" not in used_retry_kinds:\n    retry_body = self._get_retry_request_body(error, body)\n    if retry_body is not None:\n        used_retry_kinds.add(\"provider_specific\")\n        return retry_body\nreturn None\n```\n\nSo a model that *also* rejects `\"required\"` is not recovered — the failure propagates. A `named → required → auto` ladder is impossible without changing that shared gating, which would affect Mistral and every other provider using the hook. Out of scope for a bugfix; recorded in a code comment and in a test whose docstring cites the mechanism.\n\n## Verification\n\n13 new tests plus one replaced. `test_build_request_body_forced_tool_choice_downgrades_to_auto` **asserted the buggy behaviour** — an existing test asserting a bug is a finding, not an obstacle — and is now `test_build_request_body_forced_tool_choice_reaches_wire_unmodified`.\n\nMutation-tested, each confirmed failing by name:\n\n```\ndowngrade \"required\" -> \"auto\"   3 failed  (clone helper, retry hook, stream retry)\npredicate always True            4 failed  (both over-trigger guards fired)\npredicate always False           4 failed\n```\n\n```\ntests/providers/test_deepseek.py    53 passed\ntests/providers                   1064 passed, no regressions\nruff format --check                924 files already formatted\nruff check / ty check              All checks passed!\n```\n\n## Residual risks\n\n**No live DeepSeek key.** The rejection path is exercised against simulated 400s, not a real reasoning model. The predicate's word list is therefore a best match against reported error text (`\"deepseek-reasoner does not support this tool_choice\"`), not against a response I have observed. If DeepSeek's wording differs, the symptom is the old behaviour minus the silence — the 400 surfaces instead of being silently swallowed, which is still an improvement on debug-level masking.\n\n**One extra round trip** on affected models, by design — that is the cost of not branching on model names.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
