    "message": "fix(deepseek): stop silently discarding a forced tool choice\n\nA caller that demanded a specific tool got a request that no longer\ndemanded it. `_downgrade_forced_tool_choice` rewrote every Anthropic\n`tool_choice: {type:\"tool\", name:X}` to `{\"type\":\"auto\"}` while building\nthe request body, logging only at debug level. The model was then free to\nanswer in prose and call nothing -- exactly the failure a forced tool\nchoice exists to prevent -- and nothing surfaced that the demand had been\ndropped.\n\nMechanism: the downgrade was unconditional and up front, applied to every\nDeepSeek request. But DeepSeek's own API reference documents\n`tool_choice` accepting \"none\" | \"auto\" | \"required\" | a named function\nobject, so forced choice is supported for the general model surface. Only\nthe reasoning models reject it, and they do so at request time with an\nHTTP 400. Downgrading everything to protect one model class removed a\ndocumented capability from all of them.\n\nThis removes the up-front rewrite and handles the rejection reactively,\nmirroring the existing sibling pattern in mistral/client.py: a narrow\nerror predicate plus a body clone, wired through the provider's\n`_get_retry_request_body` hook, logged at WARNING rather than debug.\n\nThe forced choice now reaches the wire. If DeepSeek rejects it, the\nrequest is retried once with `tool_choice: \"required\"` -- not \"auto\" --\nso the caller's must-call-a-tool intent survives even when the\nwhich-tool half cannot be honoured. Detection is on the returned error,\nnever on the model id: DeepSeek's names have already shifted once\n(deepseek-reasoner -> deepseek-v4-pro/flash) and branching on upstream\nmodel names is banned. This also self-heals if DeepSeek lifts the\nrestriction.\n\nThe predicate requires BOTH an HTTP 400 AND text mentioning tool_choice\ntogether with a rejection word, so unrelated 400s (context length, bad\nschema, invalid model) never trigger a downgrade.\n\nKnown limitation, documented in the code: the retry hook fires at most\nonce per request. `_next_create_retry_body` adds \"provider_specific\" to\n`used_retry_kinds` and every later iteration skips the branch\n(openai_chat/provider.py:340-345), so a model that also rejects\n\"required\" is not recovered and the failure propagates. Lifting that\nwould change shared retry gating for every provider and is out of scope.\n\nVerification:\n- 13 new tests plus a replaced one. The existing\n  test_build_request_body_forced_tool_choice_downgrades_to_auto asserted\n  the buggy behaviour and is now\n  test_build_request_body_forced_tool_choice_reaches_wire_unmodified.\n- Mutation-tested: flipping the downgrade to \"auto\" killed 3 tests by\n  name; forcing the predicate always-true killed 4 including both\n  over-trigger guards; always-false killed 4.\n- tests/providers: 1064 passed, no regressions.\n- ruff format --check, ruff check, ty check: all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
